### Register a new user
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "newuser",
    "email": "newuser@example.com",
    "password": "pass123"
}

### Login
# @name login
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "newuser",
    "password": "pass123"
}

### Variables from login response
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refreshToken}}

### Logout
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Protected Route Test (Example)
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/test-protected
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


### Variables (Update after Login)
# If you need to set a token manually, replace the value below. Otherwise the requests use the `login` response token.
# @accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Update Profile with Image (use curl)
# Note: Ensure the file `test_image.png` exists in the project root.
# It's important NOT to set the multipart `Content-Type` header manually — let the client/curl set it.

# Quick curl test (recommended):
```bash
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"username":"newuser","password":"pass123"}' \
    http://localhost:3000/auth/login | node -e "const s=require('fs').readFileSync(0,'utf8'); try{console.log(JSON.parse(s).accessToken||'')}catch{console.log('')}")

curl -v -X PUT "http://localhost:3000/user/update" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
    -F "username=newuser_updated" \
    -F "image=@test_image.png"
```

# REST client note: remove manual `Content-Type` and boundary lines — use your client's file-upload UI or the curl command above.
### Update Profile with Image (REST Client / Postman / Thunder Client)
# Use your REST client's form-data mode (don't set Content-Type manually):
# - Key: `username`  Type: Text  Value: `newuser_updated`
# - Key: `image`     Type: File  Select: `test_image.png` (from project root)
# Add header `Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}` (or paste token)
# Then send `PUT http://localhost:3000/user/update`.

### Update Profile with Image URL (JSON)
# Send a JSON body with `imageUrl` instead of uploading a file.
PUT http://localhost:3000/user/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

{
    "username": "newuser_updated",
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/path/to/image.png"
}

### Get User Profile
GET http://localhost:3000/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}} 


